Spec: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/spec.md (Store: bodies and content, where content lives, writers and readers; AC13, AC14, AC18, AC19, AC21)
ADR: docs/decisions/0004-capture-store.md (klauspost/compress zstd for blobs)
Why this approach: T10's write() now takes the content items: inode check, dedup by hash, blobs on disk (an existing content row skips the file), then one transaction that inserts content rows with INSERT OR IGNORE and runs the exchange or event inserts. So a row can only ever follow its blob. Blobs go through os.CreateTemp in the target directory (0600), fsync, rename, then an fsync of the directory so the rename is durable before the row commits. One zstd.Encoder per Store, since EncodeAll is safe for concurrent use.
Alternatives rejected: writing blobs inside the transaction (holds the single writer while doing file I/O and still lets a failed rename leave a committed row if ordered wrong); checking row existence with INSERT OR IGNORE alone (would rewrite every repeated blob); skipping the directory fsync (the rename could be lost on a crash after the row is durable).
Trade-off / known limit: the existence check runs outside the transaction, so two workers can both write the same blob; they rename identical bytes over each other, which is harmless. An empty body is stored as NULL, like no body. SaveParse on an unknown exchange returns ErrNotFound (declared here for T12's reader too). Recorded in plan.md ("Details fixed in T11").
Verified by: make verify; go test -race ./internal/store (TestStore_BlobDedup incl. the blob's inode unchanged on the second save, TestStore_BlobBeforeRow via the export_test hook, TestStore_SmallContentInline incl. exactly 4096 bytes, TestStore_LargeContentBlob identity and gzip_hashed_as_sent, TestStore_OpenReaderDoesNotFailWrites with 50 writes under an open mode=ro read transaction, TestStore_SaveExchangeColumns, TestStore_SaveParse; TestStore_Permissions now also covers blobs/ and a blob file); tests first failed to build on the missing API; with the existing-row skip disabled, TestStore_BlobDedup failed on the rewritten blob, then it was restored.
